and back to your regularly scheduled

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:57.160
programming. Now, something that's very

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:59.080
similar to dubbing is what I like to

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.120
call the wrong language trap. And this

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:03.760
is where YouTube automatically generates

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:06.120
captions for your videos, and 99% of the

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:07.520
time they do a phenomenal job. They

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.920
choose the correct language and they

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.480
generate captions, and they do a pretty

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:14.240
good job. But once in a while, for some

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:16.360
reason, YouTube will get the language of

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:18.040
your video wrong. So, they might

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:20.080
generate captions in Spanish or they

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:21.680
might generate captions in Vietnamese or

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.920
something random like that when your

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.120
video is clearly in English. And of

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:28.000
course, if that happens often times the

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:29.520
algorithm is going to punish you. So,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:31.080
here are some real examples from

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:32.520
creators. This creator, for instance,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.400
posted a video in English, but the

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:36.680
auto-generated captions defaulted to

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:38.920
Vietnamese. They had no idea why. The

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:41.280
video was clearly in English, but they

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.680
asked, "Will this affect where YouTube

00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.880
shows my videos?" And the answer is yes,

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:47.600
absolutely yes. YouTube uses caption

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.440
language as a signal. It helps the

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:50.960
algorithm understand who should see your

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:52.640
video. If the captions are wrong, then

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:54.760
the recommendations are likely going to

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:56.240
be at least somewhat wrong as well, and

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:58.040
your videos will likely get pushed to

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.440
people who don't want it and held back

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:01.680
from people who do want it. And this

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:03.920
also affects the viewer experience. So,

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:06.160
if someone needs captions and they're in

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:07.280
the wrong language, then they just leave

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.880
and they're frustrated and they don't

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:11.040
come back. And all of this is going to

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:13.040
hurt your engagement metrics. So, make

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.520
sure your videos have the right captions

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.720
if auto caption is enabled, and make

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.440
sure they're of course in the right

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.520
language. Now, in order to fix this, go

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:22.240
to YouTube Studio, click content, find

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.960
the video you want to check, click the

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.000
pencil icon to edit, go to subtitles in

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:29.120
the left menu, check what language is

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.840
set for automatic captions. If it says

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.680
English automatic and you speak English,

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:34.240
you're good. If it says anything else,

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.120
change it immediately. You can also

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.320
upload manual captions if you want.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.880
That's a lot of extra work, you don't

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:41.320
have to, but you can. And that way you

00:06:38.880 --> 00:06:42.920
control exactly what YouTube sees. You

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.560
can also check your upload defaults. Go

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:46.320
to settings, then upload defaults,

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:48.640
scroll to the video details, show click

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:50.600
more, make sure your default language is

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:52.640
set correctly. And this prevents future

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:54.800
videos from having the same problem. And

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.480
honestly, don't let YouTube guess your

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:58.600
language. Tell it exactly what you're

00:06:56.480 --> 00:07:01.200
speaking. All right, number two is what

